1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,000
This is my smart bicycle tail light system.

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:09,800
The tail light stays on as I move the model forward or
backward.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,900
This is the front controller, and this is the rear light.

4
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:18,700
They can be mounted on a real bicycle.

5
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:25,700
When the bicycle is stationary, all eight LEDs are red.

6
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,200
While riding, the two center LEDs turn green.

7
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,700
The sensor detects movement as I move the model.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,500
The green center lights show people behind that the bicycle is
moving.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,700
When I stop, the tail light returns to red.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,400
The system also has turn signals.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,800
They show whether I am turning left or right.

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,300
It also has flashing hazard lights.

13
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:59,000
These warn people behind of a hazard.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,300
Another feature is automatic braking detection.

15
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:07,300
When the sensor detects a braking movement,

16
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:14,700
the red lights flash and the buzzer sounds to warn people
behind.

17
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,800
Finally, here is the emergency warning.

18
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:24,400
In this demonstration, tilting the model can trigger the SOS
warning.

19
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,700
Flashing lights and an alarm alert nearby people that help is
needed.

20
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
To clear SOS, hold both A and B for three seconds.

21
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:38,800
The emergency warning then stops.

